      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what youre saying about ethics and stuff, but im not trying to be discriminatory. im literally looking at this from a criminological perspective for my thesis. like, if we want to create better social programs or even preventative policing, we have to understand the specific behavioral patterns or environmental stressors that are statistically more prevalent in those areas. if a researcher is looking for markers like impulsivity, specific ways of communicating, or different social hierarchies that are common in high-density urban settings, isnt that just standard sociological observation? i just need help framing the questions so they look professional and academic rather than just sounding like bias.",
